            "title": "Minimum Spanning Trees & Dijkstra",
            "content": "<h3 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-blue-400\">Minimum Spanning Trees &amp; Dijkstra</h3>\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500\">CS-402 &bull; Unit 2: Greedy Method</p>\n<p class=\"mb-4 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\">Greedy graph algorithms connect or route at minimum cost.</p>\n\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6\">\n    <div class=\"bg-gray-800/90 p-5 rounded-xl border-t-4 border-blue-500 shadow-lg\">\n        <h4 class=\"text-blue-300 font-bold mb-3 text-lg\">Core Concepts</h4>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm\">\n            <li><strong>Kruskal's Algorithm:</strong> sorts edges and adds those not forming a cycle; O(E log E)</li>\n            <li><strong>Prim's Algorithm:</strong> grows the tree by the cheapest edge leaving it</li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bg-gray-800/90 p-5 rounded-xl border-t-4 border-emerald-500 shadow-lg\">\n        <h4 class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold mb-3 text-lg\">Key Points &amp; Exam Focus</h4>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm\">\n            <li><strong>Dijkstra's Algorithm:</strong> greedy shortest paths for non-negative edge weights</li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold mb-2 text-blue-400\">Concept Map</h3>\n<div class=\"mermaid bg-gray-900 p-6 rounded-lg mb-6 flex justify-center border border-gray-700 shadow-inner\">\ngraph LR\n    T[Minimum Spanning Trees and Dijkstra]\n    T --> N0[Kruskal's Algorithm]\n    T --> N1[Prim's Algorithm]\n    T --> N2[Dijkstra's Algorithm]\n    P[Prev: Huffman Coding] -.-> T\n    style T fill:#1e293b,stroke:#3b82f6,color:#fff\n    style N0 fill:#1e293b,stroke:#10b981,color:#fff\n    style N1 fill:#1e293b,stroke:#f59e0b,color:#fff\n    style N2 fill:#1e293b,stroke:#8b5cf6,color:#fff\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold mb-2 text-blue-400\">Quick Revision Table</h3>\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto mb-6\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-t border-slate-800\"><td class=\"py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-cyan-300 align-top\">Kruskal's Algorithm</td><td class=\"py-2 text-slate-300\">sorts edges and adds those not forming a cycle; O(E log E)</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-t border-slate-800\"><td class=\"py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-cyan-300 align-top\">Prim's Algorithm</td><td class=\"py-2 text-slate-300\">grows the tree by the cheapest edge leaving it</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-t border-slate-800\"><td class=\"py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-cyan-300 align-top\">Dijkstra's Algorithm</td><td class=\"py-2 text-slate-300\">greedy shortest paths for non-negative edge weights</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold mb-2 text-blue-400\">In-depth Explanation</h3>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-700 rounded-xl p-5 mb-6 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed space-y-3\">\n    <p>Greedy graph algorithms connect or route at minimum cost. Start with <strong>Kruskal's Algorithm</strong>, which is sorts edges and adds those not forming a cycle; O(E log E). Next comes <strong>Prim's Algorithm</strong>, which is grows the tree by the cheapest edge leaving it. Finally, there is <strong>Dijkstra's Algorithm</strong>, which is greedy shortest paths for non-negative edge weights.</p>\n    <p>Together, <em>Kruskal's Algorithm</em>, <em>Prim's Algorithm</em> and <em>Dijkstra's Algorithm</em> form the vocabulary examiners expect when they ask about <strong>Minimum Spanning Trees &amp; Dijkstra</strong>. Write each definition precisely, add a labelled diagram or formula where one exists, and close with an application or example.</p>\n    <p><strong>Links within Unit 2:</strong> this topic is usually read together with Greedy Strategy, Fractional Knapsack &amp; Job Sequencing and Huffman Coding; long answers on <em>Greedy Method</em> often combine them.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 border border-amber-500/30 rounded-xl p-5 mb-6 text-sm text-amber-200/90\">\n    <h4 class=\"font-bold text-amber-300 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2\">\n        <span>&#128221;</span> RGPV Exam Blueprint\n    </h4>\n    <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 leading-relaxed\">\n            <li>Define <em>Kruskal's Algorithm</em> and state where it is used. <span class=\"text-slate-500\">(2-3 marks)</span></li>\n            <li>Define <em>Prim's Algorithm</em> and state where it is used. <span class=\"text-slate-500\">(2-3 marks)</span></li>\n            <li>Define <em>Dijkstra's Algorithm</em> and state where it is used. <span class=\"text-slate-500\">(2-3 marks)</span></li>\n            <li>Differentiate between <em>Kruskal's Algorithm</em> and <em>Prim's Algorithm</em> (any four points). <span class=\"text-slate-500\">(4 marks)</span></li>\n            <li>Explain <em>Minimum Spanning Trees &amp; Dijkstra</em> with a neat labelled diagram, covering Kruskal's Algorithm, Prim's Algorithm, Dijkstra's Algorithm. <span class=\"text-slate-500\">(7 marks)</span></li>\n    </ul>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6\">\n    <div class=\"bg-gray-800/90 p-5 rounded-xl border-t-4 border-red-500 shadow-lg\">\n        <h4 class=\"text-red-300 font-bold mb-3 text-lg\">&#127909; Video Lectures</h4>\n        <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm\">\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Minimum%20Spanning%20Trees%20%26%20Dijkstra%20Analysis%20%26%20Design%20of%20Algorithms\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"text-red-300 hover:text-red-200 underline decoration-red-500/40\">&#9654; Minimum Spanning Trees & Dijkstra &mdash; full lecture</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Minimum%20Spanning%20Trees%20%26%20Dijkstra%20NPTEL\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"text-red-300 hover:text-red-200 underline decoration-red-500/40\">&#9654; Minimum Spanning Trees & Dijkstra &mdash; NPTEL / IIT lectures</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Minimum%20Spanning%20Trees%20%26%20Dijkstra%20RGPV%20CS-402%20important%20questions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"text-red-300 hover:text-red-200 underline decoration-red-500/40\">&#9654; CS-402 &mdash; RGPV exam-oriented explanation</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Analysis%20%26%20Design%20of%20Algorithms%20unit%202%20Greedy%20Method\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"text-red-300 hover:text-red-200 underline decoration-red-500/40\">&#9654; Unit 2 complete playlist: Greedy Method</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bg-gray-800/90 p-5 rounded-xl border-t-4 border-cyan-500 shadow-lg\">\n        <h4 class=\"text-cyan-300 font-bold mb-3 text-lg\">&#128218; Study Material &amp; References</h4>\n        <ul class=\"space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-300\">\n            <li><a href=\"assets/resources/cs402/notes/cs402-unit-wise-study-notes.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" download class=\"text-cyan-300 underline\">&#11015; CS-402 unit-wise study notes (PDF)</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"assets/resources/cs402/mock-papers/cs402-rgpv-model-question-paper.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" download class=\"text-cyan-300 underline\">&#11015; CS-402 RGPV model question paper (PDF)</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.rgpv.ac.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"text-cyan-300 underline\">Official RGPV scheme &amp; syllabus portal</a></li>\n        </ul>\n        <p class=\"text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 mt-3 mb-1\">Standard textbooks</p>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-xs text-gray-400\">\n            <li><em>Introduction to Algorithms</em> &mdash; Cormen, Leiserson, Rivest &amp; Stein</li>\n            <li><em>Fundamentals of Computer Algorithms</em> &mdash; Horowitz, Sahni &amp; Rajasekaran</li>\n            <li><em>Algorithm Design</em> &mdash; Kleinberg &amp; Tardos</li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n</div>",
